Observed on port/P3-03 (c2731b3, debug build as scripts/ci.sh runs it): "createOperationResult 4000 same-length picked items: 28.968879917 seconds". The test fails with "Expectation failed: elapsed < .seconds(1)". With 40,000 items the test was still running after more than 10 minutes of CPU and was killed. The reference's Set lookup takes milliseconds for the same input.

Original: `.details-row { width: 100% }` and `.details-table { min-width: 100% }` (styles.css:2875-2876, 2968-2969), so rows always fill the pane. Capture `acceptance/a13-views` (1200x760, with toggleFolderTree run after the folder loads): in Electron, 'first list row' and 'list odd row' 0..6 have frame x10 w1180, and the 'list selected bar' (Toast.jsx) also has frame x10 w1180. In Swift every one of them is x10 w892, the width from before the tree was hidden (912 pane - 2x10). In tools/capture/out/a13-views/swift/main.png the stripes and the blue selection bar stop at about 2/3 of the pane, and the selected row's Permissions value '644' is not drawn, while electron/main.png shows full-width bars with '644' on the selected row. Failing GUI test (run with `lockf -k ~/Library/Caches/filetrail-port/gui.lock env FILETRAIL_GUI_TESTS=1 swift test --filter ReviewRowWidthTests`, file Tests/FTAppKitTests/Content/ReviewRowWidthTests.swift):
